Description: see how much electricity this computer is using
 HorsePower reads the energy counters built into Intel and AMD processors and
 shows the power drawn right now, a breakdown of where it goes, the energy used
 today and the energy used since installation. A small background service
 samples the counter every second and keeps a local SQLite log, so totals stay
 correct while the window is closed. Daily totals are kept forever and minute
 samples for ninety days. An optional tariff turns energy into cost.
 .
 The breakdown separates the CPU package, the graphics card, memory, storage
 and the rest of the system, omitting any part the machine cannot measure.
 Readings cover the whole platform where a platform counter is exposed, and the
 battery on machines without RAPL. Nothing leaves the computer.
